===== piprd managed behavior =====
    71	## Managed runs
    72	
    73	`/piprd run docs/prds/prd-001.md` starts at the named PRD, then continues through the remaining `.md` files in the same directory, sorted naturally. `README.md` is ignored.
    74	
    75	For each PRD, the extension:
    76	
    77	1. sends an implementation task;
    78	2. sends a review task;
    79	3. parses the required review JSON result;
    80	4. when the review says `REVISE`, sends an advise task that analyzes the review feedback and determines the best course of action;
    81	5. sends revision tasks with both the review feedback and advisor guidance, up to `max_review_cycles` in the PRD or 5 attempts by default;
    82	6. commits approved changes;
    83	7. advances to the next PRD.
    84	
    85	Advice is enabled by default because it improves the quality of revisions. Use `--no-advise` to opt out for faster/lower-cost runs.
    86	
